Conformal prediction can be applied at two complementary scales: local and global. At the local scale, it can be used to estimate calibrated win probabilities from judge scores via maximum likelihood, which can reduce estimation error. At the global scale, it can be used to account for the residual gap between LLM-derived and human-derived Elo ratings by applying split conformal prediction to the LLM-human Elo residuals across held-out models.

