In the context of the articles discussed, cryptographic hash functions are used to construct various hash functions, such as the sponge and Davies-Meyer constructions, which are used to build hash functions from permutations and ciphers. These constructions provide a secure way to hash input data, making it difficult for attackers to reverse-engineer the original data.

